# JOURNAL — {{CAMPAIGN_TITLE}} (the campaign's working memory)

This file is what the next worker reads first: the state of the campaign's thinking, kept current by
the worker at the end of every unit and delivered whole into every spawned prompt. It is bounded by
construction — bring it up to date, do not append to it: edit what your unit changed and leave the rest
as it was. Keep it brief — every spawn pays for it — but there is no cap and nothing is cut; the driver
archives every version to `results/journal_archive/`, so nothing written here is ever lost. The record itself
lives elsewhere and is never copied here: the numbers and the one-line timeline in `results/scoreboard.tsv`
(one row per experiment — `what`, plausible range, label, an optional `note`, a `finding` where a
verdict settled something), the narrative of each experiment in `results/logbook.md` (its entry, written
by the runner; your Analysis and NEXT through `run_campaign.py --record`). Write to a peer taking over:
pass the model, not the instructions — the reasoning behind a recommendation, so the successor can
re-judge it in its own context.

